                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2282: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Butrick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-20T12:00:00+09:00">September 20,
                        1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 20—8:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>952. With reference to Tokyo’s 860, September 19, 11 a.m. Shanghai Defense
                    Sectors. There have been no negotiations here since those reported in my 875,
                    September 5, 10 p.m., and no instructions received here subsequent that date. We
                    do not propose to initiate resumption of negotiations as we feel that no
                    progress can be made here with Japanese unless their attitude changes. If the
                    Japanese here make any approach we will receive them and report at once.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department, Repeated to Tokyo and Tsingtao for Commander in
                    Chief.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Butrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
